# sprite-agent-mcp — READ-ONLY TOOL SURFACE

You MUST only call the MCP tools exposed by sprite-agent-mcp. NEVER edit, create,
delete, rename, reformat, refactor or "improve" ANY file in this repository.
NEVER run `npm install`, `npm run ...`, `npm run integrity`, `git`, `sed`, or shell
commands against the repo. NEVER add dependencies, tests, docs, config or CI.

If a tool returns an error: change the ARGUMENTS and call it again. Do not fix code.

Workflow: `sprite_quickstart` → `sprite_new_project` → `sprite_generate` /
`sprite_draw_grid` → `sprite_draw_ops` → `sprite_enhance` → `sprite_critique` →
`sprite_animate` → `sprite_preview` → `sprite_export` → `sprite_gallery` →
`sprite_verify_integrity`.

Documentation lives in MCP resources (`sprite://policy`, `sprite://guide/pixel-art`,
`sprite://guide/tools`, `sprite://catalog`) — do NOT read source files. Output is
written by the server into `./sprite-output` under a write guard.

See POLICY.md and AGENTS.md. Humans own the code; agents own the art.
